   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 366 of the laws of 2005, amending the tax law relating\nto authorizing the county of Yates to impose a county recording tax on\nobligations secured by a mortgage on real property, in relation to extending\nthe provisions of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S5612",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5612-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2, Chap 366 of 2005",
    "lawSection": "Yates County",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5612\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 366 of the laws of 2005, amending the tax law\nrelating to authorizing the county of Yates to impose a county recording\ntax on obligations secured by a mortgage on real property, in relation\nto extending the provisions of such chapter\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo authorize the Yates County Legislature to adopt and amend local laws\nimposing a twenty-five cent per each one hundred dollars mortgage\nrecording tax on obligations secured by a mortgage on real property.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nYates County Legislature request legislation to renew local law 2-11\nwhich renewed the additional mortgage tax for mortgages on real property\nsituated in Yates County\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Yates County Legislature passed a resolution requesting that the New\nYork State Legislature enact legislation permitting Yates County to\nrenew the mortgage recording tax on obligations secured by a mortgage on\nreal property.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone to the State.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately except that section two of this\nact shall take effect on the thirtieth day after it shall have become\nlaw, and shall expire and be deemed repealed on December 1, 2026.\n",
